 "notes": "Stretch 2. Line numerals: LXXXIX continues line 9 (last numeral on p.113) at the top of p.114; '10.' at start of p.114 row 2 (before χeft); '11.' in row 3 between Àusàr and Ani; '12.' in row 5 between Àmentet and maa-f. XCI: '1.' before Re of the title (p.114 last row); '2.' at start of p.115 row 2 (before baiu); '3.' in row 3 between χu and en; '4.' in row 5 between Rā and Ḥet Ḥeru. XCII: '1.' before Re (p.115 row 8). Overlines: p.114 row 7 from t'eṭ to end of row (t'eṭ ḥer ba en nub meḥ em āat erṭāu en); row 8 over śenbet-f and Àusàr only (se not overlined); XCI title overline Re…χenà-tu, then a separate short overline over em only (ba, se, Neter-χert not overlined). p.115 row 1 over t'eṭ àn only; row 5 from àr to pen; row 6 three overlines: àu-f…em, āper em, àn χenà-tuf (χu and Neter-χert not); row 7 whole row ḥer…nu; XCII title row whole row Re…em; last row hru…àn (Àusàr ān Ani not). Tiny raised vertical ticks (footnote-mark-like, but no footnote on these pages) stand at the upper right of ba (p.114 rows 3 and 7; p.115 rows 3 and 8), the ram (p.115 row 2) and χu (p.115 rows 3,4,6): not coded. On p.114 row 7 a similar short stroke over the three strokes of t'eṭ was coded Z1 (doubtful). Brackets in the hieroglyph line: [X1] in erṭāt-[t]en (p.114 row 2) and [te]n (p.114 row 4). '[uà]' (p.115 row 4) and '[and]' (row 5) are in transliteration/English only. No '……', no (sic)/(?) printed. Running heads not read."
